      "problem": "If $-2y-6=10$, then $y=${{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "First, we apply the addition principle, adding $6$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2y-6 & =10 \\\\ -2y-6+6 & =10+6 \\\\ -2y+0 & =16 \\\\ -2y & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSecond, we apply the multiplication principle, dividing both sides by $-2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2y & =16 \\\\ \\frac{-2y}{-2} & =\\frac{16}{-2} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{-2}y}{\\cancel{-2}} & =-8 \\\\ y & =-8\\end{aligned}\n$$",
